+++ b/docs/adr/0002-posts-are-drafts-until-published.md
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: stable
+entities: [Post]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/PostResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/PostPolicy.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-opus-5/1.0", at: 2026-08-18T10:34:42.659Z }
+---
+
+# Posts are drafts until published
+
+## Context
+
+Every post used to be public the moment it was saved, so an editor could
+not write across several sessions without the half-finished text being
+readable by anyone who found the URL.
+
+## Decision
+
+`posts.published` is a boolean column defaulting to `false`, so a post is
+a draft unless its author says otherwise. The create and edit forms carry
+a `published` checkbox, submitted as an optional boolean named
+`published`: absent means "draft" on create and "leave the current state
+alone" on update.
+
+Visibility is one rule — *published, or mine* — applied in three places
+in `PostController`:
+
+- `index()` and `search()` narrow their query with the `visibleTo()`
+  group, a `where(callback)` so the OR pair stays parenthesized beside
+  the keyword filter instead of being OR'd away;
+- `show()` asks `PostPolicy.view()` and turns a denial into **404**, not
+  403, so a draft is indistinguishable from an id that was never used.
+
+`update`/`destroy` keep their existing ownership checks — the flag adds
+no new authorization there. Posts written by the demo seeder are created
+published, so a seeded blog is not an empty list of drafts.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Authors see their own drafts in the post list and in search results,
+mixed in with published posts; the pages show no badge to tell the two
+apart yet, which is worth adding if drafts become common. Anything that
+reads posts outside `PostController` (a feed, an API, a sitemap) has to
+apply the same filter itself — the rule lives in the controller and the
+policy, not in a global scope on the model.
